{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Hands on In Between is a remix album from Paul van Dyk, released on 24 November 2008.","title":"Hands on in Between"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This album consists of two CDs of remixed songs featured on the original "In Between" album in 2007.","title":"Hands on in Between"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Selections from this album were remixed by various trance artists in the scene.","title":"Hands on in Between"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It also includes the winning remix from van Dyk's "Far Away Remix Competition" featured on Beatport earlier in the year.","title":"Hands on in Between"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The winning remix was promised a release, in which progressive trance producer Mateo Murphy was given the honour.","title":"Hands on in Between"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" As well as a release on the "Far Away" single, his remix made it onto this compilation too.","title":"Hands on in Between"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Seven Ways is a trance album by Paul van Dyk released on MFS in 1996 and later on Deviant Records and Mute Records.","title":"Seven Ways"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is Paul van Dyk's second studio album.","title":"Seven Ways"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Several editions include a bonus disc featuring remixes of tracks from the main disc, as well as bonus tracks.","title":"Seven Ways"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"In Between is the fifth studio album by Paul van Dyk released on 14 August 2007.","title":"In Between (Paul van Dyk album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The album features a wide range of collaborations including David Byrne of Talking Heads, Jessica Sutta of the Pussycat Dolls, Ashley Tomberlin of Luminary, Alex M.O.R.P.H., Lo-Fi Sugar, Rea Garvey of Reamonn, Ryan Merchant and Wayne Jackson.","title":"In Between (Paul van Dyk album)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The latter had collaborated earlier with Paul van Dyk on the song "The Other Side".","title":"In Between (Paul van Dyk album)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The album also features a vocal sample of Ben Lost from Probspot's "Blows My Mind" on the song "Another Sunday".","title":"In Between (Paul van Dyk album)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Out There and Back is the third studio album by Paul van Dyk.","title":"Out There and Back"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was released in 2000 and is the first album released on his own Vandit record label.","title":"Out There and Back"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It can be seen as Paul van Dyk's breakthrough album.","title":"Out There and Back"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Several editions include a bonus CD.","title":"Out There and Back"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""The Other Side" is a single released on Paul van Dyk's second DJ mix album "The Politics of Dancing 2".","title":"The Other Side (Paul van Dyk song)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Paul van Dyk wrote the song in retort to the devastating tsunami which hit southeast Asia on 26 December 2004.","title":"The Other Side (Paul van Dyk song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Van Dyk believes it is important to recognise that many thousands of people were affected by this tragedy, and lost loved ones.","title":"The Other Side (Paul van Dyk song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" "The Other Side" portrays the feeling of still being with a person, in one's thoughts, who has died.","title":"The Other Side (Paul van Dyk song)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It expresses the faith and aspiration of seeing that person again on "the other side".","title":"The Other Side (Paul van Dyk song)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""For An Angel" is a trance debut track by German DJ Paul van Dyk.","title":"For an Angel"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His most famous track, it was initially released in 1994 as a track on "45 RPM" on the MFS record label, which was van Dyk's first studio album.","title":"For an Angel"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was later reworked and re-released in 1998 as "E-Werk Remix" on Deviant Records, a homage to the E-Werk nightclub where van Dyk used to be the resident DJ, the song reached number-one on the UK Dance Chart for several weeks.","title":"For an Angel"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Since its release the track has become one of the most influential and greatest trance tracks of all time.","title":"For an Angel"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It was voted by "Mixmag" readers as the eighth greatest dance record of all time.","title":"For an Angel"}],"peer_messages":["Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"Hands on In Between is a remix album from Paul van Dyk, released on 24 November 2008.","title":"Hands on in Between"}
